# The gateway's documentation as an MCP server (package
# mcp-gateway-fs-server): agents read the user guide, the architecture and
# the changelog installed with the gateway, without the network, to help
# with its configuration. Read-only, as a throwaway user, in the
# mcpsrv_docs_t domain, which reads /usr and nothing of the user's.
# Users need the shipped role gateway-docs-reader (or a role naming the
# server). To change it, copy this file to
# /etc/mcp-gateway/servers.d/gateway-docs.yaml; an empty file of that
# name disables it.
version: 1
name: gateway-docs
command: ["@LIBEXECDIR@/mcp-servers/mcp-server-fs", "--read-only", "--root", "@DATADIR@/mcp-gateway/docs",
  "--instructions", "The documentation of mcp-gateway, the MCP gateway this server and the others run behind, for the installed version. Start with README.md: which file answers which question, and where each common error message is explained. user-guide/ has 13 chapters (chapter N is user-guide/NN-*.md; 10-operations has the troubleshooting and the self-check, 11-reference the options, files and limits), architecture.md the design and its decisions, CHANGELOG.md what changed and how to upgrade. To answer, search first and read only around the match: search_text (query, path) gives the matching lines with file and line number; then read_text_file with offset and limit (say 40 lines from a little before the match). For a broad question without a precise term (how does approval work?), outline_file (path) lists a file's headings with their line numbers and sizes: read the one section with read_text_file (offset: its line, limit: its lines). Read architecture.md and CHANGELOG.md this way, never whole; read a chapter whole only when the question needs all of it. search_files finds file names, not text. The configuration on this machine is not here: the server gateway-admin shows it (show_config) and checks it (check_config, doctor)."]
selinux_type: mcpsrv_docs_t
run_as: dynamic
network: false
# Landlock: the documentation, the system's programs and configuration;
# no home directory.
landlock:
  read: ["@DATADIR@/mcp-gateway/docs"]
